<%# The river itself, with a day spine through it (D-reader-density).

    Four hundred rows that all read "1h" gave the list no shape — the age
    column, two characters wide and well-judged for a laptop, does no work
    when a whole sweep lands at once, and there was no sense of how far back
    you had got or of a floor you could reach. A heading per day costs one
    row per group and gives the pile a bottom.

    Locals: page. %>
<div class="reader-river">
  <% last_day = nil %>
  <% page.items.each do |item| %>
    <% day = reader_day_label(item.published_on) %>
    <% if day != last_day %>
      <h2 class="reader-day"><%= day %></h2>
      <% last_day = day %>
    <% end %>
    <%= render "reader/item", item: item, filter: @river.filter %>
  <% end %>
</div>
